{"hash":"bf89ba1b28a8394b","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":87.32,"said":"Om Namah Shivaya. Come, walk with me through the gate. Can you feel the salt in the wind? We are on the coast of Saurashtra, on the road that runs from Dwarka, Lord Krishna’s city, out toward the island of Bet Dwarka. Look around you: flat, dry land, thorny babul trees, a wide open sky. The Shiva Purana remembers this country very differently, as Darukavana, a rich forest on the shore of the western ocean, sixteen yojanas across. It also remembers who ruled that forest, and you will hear about them in a moment. First, the temple ahead. Its walls are new, though its Lord is very old. In the 1990s a devotee named Gulshan Kumar came here on a pilgrimage to the twelve Jyotirlingas. Born in Delhi, the son of a fruit-juice seller, he had built the music company T-Series. Accounts of the temple say he found the old shrine in poor repair and paid for a new one, begun around 1996. He did not live to see it finished. He died in 1997, and his family completed the work. Now look up, to the north. Someone very large is waiting for us.\n\nDid you know? Close by is Gopi Talav, a lake that tradition links with the gopis, the cowherd women devoted to Lord Krishna.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":1037},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":1053,"end":1163}],"words":[[0.098,0.204,0,2],[0.314,0.312,3,8],[0.639,0.553,9,16],[2.127,0.445,18,22],[2.764,0.3,24,28],[3.077,0.192,29,33],[3.281,0.132,34,36],[3.425,0.192,37,44],[3.63,0.096,45,48],[3.738,0.409,49,53],[5.072,0.192,55,58],[5.276,0.096,59,62],[5.385,0.24,63,67],[5.637,0.084,68,71],[5.733,0.349,72,76],[6.094,0.084,77,79],[6.19,0.108,80,83],[6.31,0.433,84,88],[7.56,0.204,90,92],[7.776,0.096,93,96],[7.885,0.12,97,99],[8.017,0.084,100,103],[8.113,0.361,104,109],[8.486,0.132,110,112],[8.63,0.721,113,123],[9.531,0.108,125,127],[9.651,0.072,128,131],[9.736,0.312,132,136],[10.06,0.192,137,141],[10.264,0.312,142,146],[10.589,0.192,147,151],[10